{title: 504 - Lord Jesus, Think on Me}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #504 • SOUTHWELL • 12.14}
{lyricist: Synesius of Cyrene}
{composer: Damon's Psalmes}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 504}
{meta: tune SOUTHWELL}
{meta: meter 12.14}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C/G]Lord [G]Jesus, [D7/C]think [Bm]on [C/G]me, And [G]purge away [F#dim]my [G]sin;
[G]From [D/A]earth-born [C/G]passions [G]set me [F#dim]free, [G/D]And [D7/C]make [Em/B]me [Bm]pure within.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C/G]Lord [G]Jesus, [D7/C]think [Bm]on [C/G]me, With [G]care and woe [F#dim]oppressed;
[G]Let [D/A]me Thy [C/G]loving [G]servant [F#dim]be, [G/D]And [D7/C]taste [Em/B]Thy [Bm]promised [C/G]rest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C/G]Lord [G]Jesus, [D7/C]think [Bm]on [C/G]me, Nor [G]let me go [F#dim]astray;
[G]Through darkness [D/A]and [C/G]perplexity [F#dim]Point [G/D]Thou [D7/C]the [Em/B]heavenly [C/G]way.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C/G]Lord [G]Jesus, [D7/C]think [Bm]on [C/G]me, That [G]I may sing [F#dim]above
[G]To [D/A]Father, [C/G]Spirit, [G]and to [F#dim]Thee, [G/D]The [D7/C]strains [Em/B]of [Bm]praise and [C/G]love.
{end_of_verse}
